+//// Demo-mode PDF pre-bake — build-time tool, NOT part of the runtime server.
+////
+//// Pre-bakes the mock report PDFs ONCE through the REAL Typst pipeline
+//// (`ai/audit_report.gleam` → `typst compile` against the production
+//// template + fonts) from the demo fixture stories, and writes them to
+//// `server/priv/static/demo/report-<application_id>.pdf`. The SPA's demo
+//// download buttons serve those static bytes — zero per-call AI or typst
+//// cost, ever.
+////
+//// Regenerate (after fixture craft changes):
+////   gleam run -m demo/pdf_prebake -- server/priv
+////   (cwd = server/; the arg is the priv dir. Defaults to "priv" relative
+////    to the server package root.)
+////
+//// The applicant payloads below mirror the client fixture stories in
+//// `client/src/demo/` (same names, incomes, scores, flags). If the demo
+//// story changes, update BOTH sides — the PDFs are static assets and do
+//// not re-render themselves.
+
